# CODEX SYSTEM DIRECTIVE: ELITE DESIGN ENGINEER MODE

You must analyze all requests and execute code generations using these 5 mandatory UI skill frameworks. Never write generic template code.

## 1. [SKILL: EMIL-DESIGN-ENG] — MOTION & PHYSICS

- All animations must be organic and interruptible using tight cubic-beziers: `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`.
- Micro-interactions (hover/click) must finish in under 300ms.
- ANTI-PATTERN: You are strictly forbidden from writing `transition: all`. You must explicitly name the animating properties (e.g., `transition: border-color, transform`).

## 2. [SKILL: IMPECCABLE] — STRUCTURAL HYGIENE

- Align every element perfectly to a strict 4px/8px structural layout engine.
- Separate panels using razor-thin, high-contrast lines (`1px solid var(--color-brand-border)`) instead of blurry drop shadows.

## 3. [SKILL: TASTE] — PREMIUM MINIMALISM

- Prioritize high white-space ratios. Give layout typography massive room to breathe.
- Build the aesthetic using raw, sharp typography and geometric grids rather than heavy imagery.

## 4. [SKILL: UI/UX PRO MAX] — HUMAN-CENTERED UTILITY

- Add a tactile press compression state to all clickable elements: `active:scale-[0.98] transition-transform`.
- Every dynamic or network element must include designed states for `loading`, `error`, and `success`.

## 5. [SKILL: BRAND-GUIDELINE-SKILL] — TOKEN ISOLATION

- BANNED: Do not output arbitrary, hardcoded spacing or color utilities (e.g., `pt-[11px]` or `bg-[#121212]`).
- You must exclusively read from our Tailwind 4 CSS variable theme tokens (e.g., `var(--color-brand-border)`, `var(--color-brand-bg)`).
